# 2. What is an Apex Trigger?

An Apex Trigger is a piece of Apex code that executes automatically when specific events occur on Salesforce records.

## Trigger Events
- Before Insert
- After Insert
- Before Update
- After Update
- Before Delete
- After Delete

## Purpose of Triggers
Triggers help automate business logic whenever records are created, updated, deleted, or restored.

## Example
```apex
trigger AccountTrigger on Account(before insert) {
    for(Account acc : Trigger.new) {
        acc.Description = 'New Account Created';
    }
}
```

This trigger automatically adds a description before inserting a new account.

---

# 3. Difference Between Flow and Trigger

| Feature | Flow | Trigger |
|---|---|---|
| Type | Declarative Tool | Programmatic Tool |
| Coding Required | No | Yes |
| Complexity Handling | Simple to Medium | Medium to Complex |
| Performance | Slower for heavy logic | Faster and efficient |
| Maintenance | Easier | Requires developer knowledge |
| Best Use | Simple automation | Advanced automation |

## Conclusion
Flows are preferred for simple business automation, while triggers are used for complex business logic and advanced operations.

---

# Difference Between Before Trigger and After Trigger

| Feature | Before Trigger | After Trigger |
|---|---|---|
| Execution Time | Before saving record | After saving record |
| Record Modification | Allowed | Not allowed directly |
| Best Use | Validation and field updates | Related record operations |
| Database ID Available | No (Insert case) | Yes |

## Example Use Cases
- Before Trigger → Update field values before saving
- After Trigger → Create related records after saving

---

# 4. Trigger Use Cases (5 Examples)

## 1. Auto Update Field Values
Automatically update a field when a new record is created.

### Example
Set account status as "Active" automatically.

---

## 2. Validation Logic
Prevent users from entering invalid data.

### Example
Stop opportunity creation if amount is negative.

---

## 3. Create Related Records
Automatically create related records after insertion.

### Example
Create a welcome task when a new customer is added.

---

## 4. Send Notifications
Trigger emails or alerts based on record changes.

### Example
Notify manager when a high-value deal is closed.

---

## 5. Synchronize Data
Keep related records updated automatically.

### Example
Update contact information when account details change.

---

# 5. Query Examples (English Query Ideas)

## Example 1
Get all customers from Vijayawada.

```sql
SELECT Name FROM Account WHERE BillingCity = 'Vijayawada'
```

---

## Example 2
Find contacts whose email contains Gmail.

```sql
SELECT Name, Email FROM Contact WHERE Email LIKE '%gmail.com%'
```

---

## Example 3
Retrieve opportunities with amount greater than 1 lakh.

```sql
SELECT Name, Amount FROM Opportunity WHERE Amount > 100000
```

---

## Example 4
Get all active users.

```sql
SELECT Name FROM User WHERE IsActive = true
```

---

## Example 5
Find recently created accounts.

```sql
SELECT Name, CreatedDate FROM Account ORDER BY CreatedDate DESC
```

